Test requirements that are not packaged for OpenIndiana: pip (only asked
for on Python >= 3.12; there is no pip for 3.14), pygame and pygame-ce,
xlib (python-xlib) and glfw.  The tests that need them are deselected in
python-integrate-project.conf.

tox.ini: the test command of the accel0 environments (without
PyOpenGL-accelerate, which is not packaged) also for the plain py$(PYV)
environment that tox-current-env runs.

https://github.com/mcfletch/pyopengl/issues/180 (tox.ini and
test-requirements.txt are missing from the sdist, so they come from the
GitHub tarball)

--- pyopengl-3.1.10/test-requirements.txt.orig
+++ pyopengl-3.1.10/test-requirements.txt
@@ -1,10 +1,4 @@
 tox
-pip >= 23 ; python_version >= '3.12'
 pytest
 setuptools >= 42
-pygame < 2.1.3; python_version < '3.11'
-pygame-ce >= 2.1.3; python_version >= '3.11'
---only-binary pygame,pygame-ce
 psutil
-xlib
-glfw
\ No newline at end of file
--- pyopengl-3.1.10/tox.ini.orig
+++ pyopengl-3.1.10/tox.ini
@@ -23,4 +23,4 @@
 #install_command = pip install -I {opts} {packages}
 commands=
     accel1: python -m pytest -sv -rxXs {posargs:tests/ accelerate/tests}
-    accel0: python -m pytest -sv -rxXs {posargs:tests/}
+    python -m pytest -sv -rxXs {posargs:tests/}
